From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ddr: hold DDR3 RESET# low for 200 us

Backport from sophgo/fsbl 9876d6e6b105a594aa42fc895ec34f7f8927230d
("fsbl: weekly rls 2026.10.28"): JESD79-3 requires RESET# low for at least
200 us after power is stable; the pinned FSBL releases it after about 40 us.
---
diff --git a/plat/cv181x/ddr/ddr_sys.c b/plat/cv181x/ddr/ddr_sys.c
--- a/plat/cv181x/ddr/ddr_sys.c
+++ b/plat/cv181x/ddr/ddr_sys.c
@@ -1923,6 +1923,13 @@ void cvx16_INT_ISR_08(void)
 
 	//----------------------------------------------------
 	cvx16_ddr_phy_power_on_seq2();
+	// JESD79-3 requires RESET# to remain low for at least 200us after
+	// VDD is stable. On this platform the RESET# pad is driven low once
+	// the PHY output stage is enabled (power_on_seq1/seq2) and released
+	// only after dfi_init_complete lets the DDRC init FSM run. Holding
+	// 200us here lengthens the RESET# low pulse accordingly (measured
+	// on board: 40us -> 230+us), clearing the spec minimum with margin.
+	udelay(200);
 	cvx16_set_dfi_init_complete();
 }
 
